# fixedbugs, defect 563, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 204's R1), the
# shape beside the repair.
#
# `narrow`'s unit reads its own group's `fixedbugs-563-skew.h`, and
# `fixedbugs-563-wide.h` too, for the `wide.Wh` it spells, a header that
# defines the macro `skew.h` lays `Sk` out wide under. A module's own
# groups' headers come first in its unit, in the order they are written,
# and another module's record after them, so `Sk` is narrow as `narrow`
# reads it. Until 2026-10-10 a unit's records were read in declaration
# order across modules, and `Sk.a: i32` was refused, *`Sk.a` is `long
# long`*, in either order of the two `use` lines (panel 238's
# compiler-engineer, on the compiler of `55d20a362`), so the case guards in
# the one order the compiler walks them in since that sitting.
use fixedbugs563/narrow
use fixedbugs563/wide

function main()
    print(narrow.total(x: wide.make(v: 4)))
